course: dictionary
lesson: 2183
title: Cosmetic: looks, not how it works
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cosmetic describes something done to make a thing look better, not to make it work better. Make-up, face cream and lipstick are cosmetics. Test it with a sentence: «The new paint is a cosmetic change to the old bike.» The bike still does the same job; it just looks different.
explain: Read the clues around the word. In «Had some work done», the meaning is about how a person looks, and cosmetic surgery is an operation to change looks. Ask yourself: does this change how something works, or only how it looks? If it only changes the look, cosmetic fits.
explain: Words can also carry a hint of criticism. When people call a fix cosmetic, they often mean it hides a problem instead of solving it. A cosmetic fix to a broken door might paint it, but the lock still does not work. Check the context before you decide what the word means.
fact: Cosmetic is an adjective; cosmetics is a noun, usually used in the plural.
fact: «Cosmetic» means done only to improve how something looks, not how it works.
fact: «Cosmetic surgery» is an operation to change how someone looks.
fact: «Cosmetics» are things like make-up, face cream and lipstick that people put on to look nicer.
fact: «Purely cosmetic» means done only for looks, with no other purpose.
exercise: «The shop has a cosmetics counter full of lipstick and face cream.» What are cosmetics? | Food cooked in a pan | *Things like make-up and face cream that people use to look nicer | Books about old castles | Tools for fixing bicycles
exercise: «The new paint is a purely cosmetic change; the bike still has the same broken brakes.» What does purely cosmetic mean? | *Only changes how it looks, not how it works | Makes it lighter to carry | Changes how it works, very quickly | Makes it sound louder
exercise: Which phrase means an operation to change how someone looks? | bicycle repair | face cream | cosmetics counter | *cosmetic surgery
test: Ava says a cosmetic change to a car fixes the engine. Is she right? | Yes, the car goes faster | *No, it only changes how the car looks | No, cars cannot be changed at all | Yes, the engine is fixed
test: Which word is an adjective meaning done only to improve looks? | surgery | *cosmetic | counter | cosmetics
exam: Dad says the new sign is cosmetic, not the real fix. What does a real fix do that a cosmetic change does not? | It makes something look nicer | *It changes how something works | It covers up a mark | It changes only its colour
